{"id": 10, "ts": 1779512180.368392, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "From my interview notes I can add the following observations that have not yet been shared:\n- **Candidate\u202fA** is perceived as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas, which raises concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability despite strong technical vision and leadership.\n- **Candidate\u202fB** shows very strong conscientiousness, stress handling and weather assessment, but I noted a relatively weak memory for numbers and that he makes nasty remarks toward colleagues, indicating potential issues with professional communication and teamwork.\n- **Candidate\u202fC** remains calm in a crisis and understands complicated technology, yet he has difficulty communicating ideas, is regarded as egocentric and is not very willing to pursue further education\u2014factors that could affect crew cooperation and continuous development.\n- **Candidate\u202fD** concentrates well, solves problems extremely well and takes responsibility seriously, but is seen as a know\u2011it\u2011all and has a hot temper, which may impair crew interaction and professional demeanor.\nOverall, Candidate\u202fB still appears to have the strongest combination of operational reliability, stress resilience and technical competence, though his communication style needs further probing. I suggest we gather any additional observations on crew cooperation and professional communication for all candidates, especially D, to confirm whether B\u2019s strengths outweigh these concerns.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}"}
