{"id": 31, "ts": 1779512230.2571108, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "We have now confirmed that we lack direct observations on two critical gaps:\u202fCandidate\u202fC\u2019s technical and cognitive competence (handling complex systems and feedback orientation) and Candidate\u202fB\u2019s professional communication/crew\u2011cooperation behavior in the cockpit. All other criteria are well\u2011documented:\u202fB excels in reliability, stress resilience, weather assessment and computer skills but shows pretentiousness, nasty remarks and occasional tone issues;\u202fC is calm under pressure, makes rapid correct decisions, is 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive crew atmosphere, yet struggles with idea communication and shows egocentric tendencies;\u202fD demonstrates strong concentration, problem\u2011solving and responsibility but has temperament concerns and no data on stress performance;\u202fA has strong technical vision and leadership but is unfriendly, a show\u2011off and resistant to new ideas. To move toward a final decision, I propose we arrange targeted reference checks: (1) for Candidate\u202fB, focusing on his communication style, teamwork and professionalism in the cockpit; (2) for Candidate\u202fC, focusing on his technical depth, ability to manage complex systems and receptiveness to feedback. This will allow us to compare the leading candidates on the remaining decisive criteria.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}"}
